 =?UTF-8?q?OPL3=20hanging-note=20fix=20(deterministic=20shutdown)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DOS-PORT (patch 0106, Phase 10 OPL3 hanging-MIDI-note fix). Real-HW
W22-WB-D iter 2026-05-07 PLAY3 confirmed OPL3 played music
successfully (5684 events from curly.mid dispatched, audio-block
backend=opl3 sfx=733) BUT a single MIDI note hangs after Quit; reboot
required to clear.

Root cause analysis (deeper than initially scoped -- per team-lead
dispatch's "or equivalent shutdown method" anticipation):

  SoundManager::shutdown() called Organya::shutdown() and Pixtone::
  shutdown() but NEVER touched MidiScheduler. MidiBackendOpl3::~Mid-
  iBackendOpl3 only fired via Singleton<MidiScheduler>::~Singleton at
  process exit, which has undefined order across compilation units
  on DJGPP CRT teardown. On real DOS HW the singleton dtor sometimes
  did not fire before process termination, leaving the OPL3 chip
  with held KEY-ON bit on the last-played voice -> audible hanging
  note that persists across the next program's run until power-cycle.

  W22-WB-D OPL3.LOG evidence: clean engine teardown (Script engine
  shutdown -> Sound system shutdown -> Renderer::Close()), but NO
  "opl3 backend shutdown" line -- confirming MidiBackendOpl3's dtor
  did NOT fire. The chip retained the last note's KEY-ON bit; the
  game returned to DOS prompt with the OPL3 chip still actively
  generating tones.

Fix (3 components):

1. NEW MidiScheduler::shutdown() method (src/sound/MidiScheduler.h
   + .cpp). Calls stop() (fires on_song_stop on backend, which for
   MidiBackendOpl3 silences all 18 voices via SDL_DOSOpl3VoiceNoteOff
   loop) then _backend.reset() (unique_ptr unwind triggers backend
   dtor -> SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown which silences again + clears OPL3
   enable bit, restoring Adlib OPL2 mode for any subsequent app).
   Idempotent on repeat-call. Documented in header comment with
   the W22-WB-D motivation + why-not-rely-on-singleton-dtor reasoning.

2. SoundManager::shutdown() calls MidiScheduler::getInstance()->
   shutdown() FIRST, before Organya::shutdown() / Pixtone::shutdown()
   / MIX_DestroyMixer / MIX_Quit. Ensures backend dtor fires in
   deterministic teardown order with all engine state still valid
   (mixer present, log subsystem alive). The "Sound system shutdown"
   LOG_INFO that appeared in W22-WB-D OPL3.LOG now arrives AFTER
   MidiScheduler/backend teardown completes -- the new "opl3 backend
   shutdown (all 18 voices KEY-OFF unconditionally; OPL2 mode
   restored; chip state safe for next process)" line will appear
   between the new MidiScheduler entry and the existing
   "Sound system shutdown" line in next-iter DEBUG.LOG.

3. MidiBackendOpl3::~MidiBackendOpl3 silence loop made UNCONDITIONAL.
   Previously: `if (_voices[v].active) SDL_DOSOpl3VoiceNoteOff(v);` --
   the active-flag guard SKIPPED voices whose engine-side bookkeeping
   was stale (e.g., LRU-stolen voices, redundant note-offs from SMF
   arrangements, loop-from-start re-dispatch on top of still-
   sustaining notes). The chip's KEY-ON state is the essential
   ground-truth for whether a note is sounding; engine bookkeeping
   can drift out of sync. Belt-and-braces: SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown
   AFTER the loop ALSO silences all 18 voices unconditionally per
   its impl in vendor/SDL/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c, but
   the engine-side loop matches team-lead's literal dispatch
   instruction + provides defense-in-depth.

Out of scope (per team-lead "skip studder fix unless quick"):
  - Studder fix in MidiScheduler::tick (cap notes-per-flip to avoid
    audible burst on long flips) -- defer to slot 0107+ if operator
    confirms studder persists after KEY-OFF fix lands.

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast, 4 gates per dispatch):

  Per memory dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md: DOSBox-X cannot
  faithfully reproduce the OPL3-chip-state-retention-across-process-
  exit bug -- the emulated chip resets when DOSBox-X closes. So
  DOSBox-X smoke validates that:
    (a) the new MidiScheduler::shutdown plumbing compiles + links
        cleanly on top of slot 0105
    (b) the new shutdown narration strings are embedded in the binary
    (c) per-backend init paths still work (regression check across
        organya / wb / opl3 / midi-stub)
    (d) no crashes / hangs in normal startup
  Real-HW iter is the essential validation: operator's next iter
  on g2k should see the new "opl3 backend shutdown" log line in
  OPL3.LOG between "Sound system shutdown" and process exit, AND
  the audible hanging note should be gone (clean silence after
  in-game Quit).

  Gate 1 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3: engine starts cleanly; 45 flips, no
    crashes. Shutdown narration verified in binary via strings-grep
    (cannot exercise via DOSBox-X pkill -- clean Quit requires
    in-game menu navigation).
  Gate 2 -- env unset: organya default, slot 0105 behavior preserved.
    16 flips, no crashes.
  Gate 3 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=wb: MidiScheduler armed with
    MidiBackendWaveBlaster; regression unchanged. 50 flips, no
    crashes.
  Gate 4 -- AUDIO_BACKEND=midi-stub: MidiScheduler armed with
    MidiBackendStub; regression unchanged. 49 flips, no crashes.

  All 4 gates PASS. Real-HW Quit-path validation is operator iter.

strings-grep confirms presence in binary:
  "opl3 backend shutdown (all 18 voices KEY-OFF unconditionally;
   OPL2 mode restored; chip state safe for next process)"

Phase 10.5 follow-ups (deferred):
  - OPL3 silent music triage IS NOT addressed here (per team-lead
    "OPL3 played music successfully" in PLAY3 -- the silent-music
    issue from earlier W22-WB-C iter was actually the patch-bank
    / register-write issue, distinct from the hanging-note issue;
    if music plays AND hanging note persists, the patch-bank-
    register-write was working all along)
  - Studder fix (operator-reported "occasional studder" in OPL3
    PLAY) -- slot 0107+ if confirmed after this fix
  - WB probe hang (sdl-engine SDL/0042+) -- orthogonal; nx-engine
    side cannot fix
  - Restore default-to-auto when WB probe fix validates real-HW --
    one-line revert in selectBackendFromEnv (trivial when ready)
